---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/site/PageHead.astro';
import TriggerChart from '../components/site/TriggerChart.astro';
import LivingMark from '../components/site/LivingMark.astro';
import { getPocs } from '../lib/pocs';
const reunion = getPocs()[0];
---

<Site
    title="Trigger audit for parametric insurance · Skaraz Data"
    description="A fixed-scope second opinion on a parametric trigger, about two weeks: backtest, basis risk, data sources, and a check that the code follows the policy wording. From EUR 6,000."
>
    <PageHead
        label="Service · trigger audit · from EUR 6,000"
        title="A second opinion on your trigger before you sign, renew or pay."
        lede="A fixed scope, about two weeks, and a written answer to one question: does this index pay when it should, and only then? The same format covers index design and feasibility for a new peril."
    >
        <a slot="cta" class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing">See prices</a>
    </PageHead>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">What I check</p>
                <h2>Four things, each with a finding you can act on.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="grid cols-4">
                <div class="card reveal" style="--i:0"><p class="num chk">01</p><h3>Backtest</h3><p class="muted small">The index rerun over every season the data allows, against documented losses where they exist.</p></div>
                <div class="card reveal" style="--i:1"><p class="num chk">02</p><h3>Basis risk</h3><p class="muted small">Missed events, false payouts, and the gap between index severity and real damage.</p></div>
                <div class="card reveal" style="--i:2"><p class="num chk">03</p><h3>Data sources</h3><p class="muted small">Latency, known defects, licence terms, and whether a fallback source is written in.</p></div>
                <div class="card reveal" style="--i:3"><p class="num chk">04</p><h3>Wording to code</h3><p class="muted small">Does the code compute what the policy says, including edge cases and rounding?</p></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--tint">
        <div class="wrap two">
            <div class="stack reveal" style="--stack:1.1rem">
                <p class="label label--index">An example finding</p>
                <h2>La Réunion: the trigger catches most bleaching years, and pays in some it shouldn’t.</h2>
                <p class="lede">Over 2009 to 2024 the Degree Heating Weeks index caught 5 of the 6 documented bleaching years and missed 2015. It also paid in 2009 and 2018, with no documented mass bleaching. That gap is basis risk, and an audit puts a number on it before money moves.</p>
                <p><a class="link" href={`/showcase/${reunion.slug}`}>Read the La Réunion report <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
            </div>
            <div class="reveal chart-col" style="--i:1"><TriggerChart series={reunion.series} height={300} />{reunion.mark && <LivingMark mark={reunion.mark} size={132} />}</div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="section-head reveal">
                <p class="label label--index">How the two weeks run</p>
                <h2>From your documents to a written verdict.</h2>
            </div>
            <ol class="timeline">
                <li class="reveal" style="--i:0"><span class="num">Day 1</span><div><h3>Kick-off</h3><p class="muted">Policy wording, term sheet, index spec and any code you have. One hour call.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal" style="--i:1"><span class="num">Days 2 to 7</span><div><h3>Rebuild and backtest</h3><p class="muted">I rebuild the index independently from the named data and rerun it over the full record.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal" style="--i:2"><span class="num">Days 8 to 9</span><div><h3>Findings</h3><p class="muted">Basis-risk numbers, data issues and wording-to-code gaps, each ranked by what it would cost you.</p></div></li>
                <li class="reveal" style="--i:3"><span class="num">Day 10</span><div><h3>Report and call</h3><p class="muted">A written report, the code I used, and a call to walk through it.</p></div></li>
            </ol>
            <p class="muted small note">If the audit finds the trigger is sound, the report says so plainly. Fixed-price work: 30 to 50% on signature. Engineering and calculation, not actuarial sign-off.</p>
            <p class="go"><a class="btn" href="/scope" data-umami-event="scope-audit">Scope an audit <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
        </div>
    </section>
</Site>

<style>
    .chk { color: var(--index); font-weight: 500; font-size: 0.8125rem; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .card h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .two { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr); gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px); align-items: start; }
    .chart-col { display: grid; gap: 32px; }
    .go { margin-top: 28px; }
    .two > * { min-width: 0; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .two { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
    .timeline { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; }
    .timeline li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 24px; padding-block: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .timeline li > span { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--index); font-weight: 500; padding-top: 3px; }
    .timeline li div { display: grid; gap: 6px; }
    @media (max-width: 560px) { .timeline li { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 6px; } }
    .note { margin-top: 24px; }
</style>
